column5:
Re-document with Markdown support enabled (changes

indentation and prepends another `\` to `\` occurrences
).

add `stat = "R2"` to the tests;

also take into account that `stat = "rmse"` does not need a PRNG seed anymore
(and should produce a point estimate between the CI bounds)

Fix `tests/testthat/test_project.R` (due to the changes in `args_prj_vs`, see commit
"`setup.R`: Make the code for the projection from "vsel" objects more robust."
).

add `stat = "R2"` to the tests;

also take into account that `stat = "rmse"` does not need a PRNG seed anymore
(and should produce a point estimate between the CI bounds)

make "Projecting onto 1" easier to understand by using "Projecting onto `~ 1`";

this is done not only for the intercept-only model, but for all submodel
formulas

add function `get_use_progressr()` to avoid redundancies;

also introduce global option `projpred.use_progressr` so that all users (even
those with `progressr` installed) may refrain from using `progressr`;
also handle the export of `use_progressr`

`project()`: Move the error for `"datafit"`s to the beginning (
otherwise, `cv_search = FALSE` causes the error "Please provide an `object` of class "vsel" or use `cv_search = TRUE`."
).

`test_proj_pred.R`: Continue simplifying/generalizing the `proj_predict()` tests in the same way as the `proj_linpred()` tests (now: test

"`object` of class \"projection\" works"
).

Remove `stopifnot(length(tstsetups) > 0)` lines (since testthat throws a "skip" message if a test is empty). `proj_linpred()` tests: Continue re-organizing/simplifying the `object` tests (now: tests

"`object` of class \"vsel\" [...]"
).

Avoid the `preprocess_data()` call in `fit_glmer_callback()` since:
  - the scaling of predictors changes their regression coefficients;
  - `preprocess_data()` is not adopted to categorical predictors;
  - `preprocess_data()`'s implementation for interactions is probably incorrect.

`proj_linpred()` tests: Continue re-organizing/simplifying the `object` tests (now: test

"`object` of (informal) class \"proj_list\" (created manually) works"
)

Replace `SW()` by `suppressMessages()` (there
was no need for the extra features of `SW()` and it even made things more complicated
).

Fix an issue with `rstanarm:::kfold.stanreg()` again (
"again" because it was already fixed before the new `fits` and `refmods` structure
).

REFACTOR: Split `encapsulate` function into two variants.

The first variant preserves the subdiagram inside a nested diagram;
the second discards it and inserts an atomic box.
